6295324 1111 #uuid "2052cef9-31f9-59eb-a157-68a3c4019d85" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295326 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1089 "q-317945" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1100 "Let $a=⟨2{x}^{2},-4⟩$ and $b=⟨8,4⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x>0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1113 #uuid "4a8b5a23-ade1-5e2d-9cfe-f55808f3f82d" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295325 1145 "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\cdot 8+(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16{x}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ 16{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $x>0.$ Therefore, $x=1.$" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295327 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295328 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1041 "field-1" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295327 13194139534558 true] [17592186295326 1110 #uuid "240955df-3d58-5743-a358-3e2c195bafc7" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295327 1034 "1" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534558 true] [17592186295327 1111 #uuid "19382e00-ca59-50b9-84d8-0478e4b121bf" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295328 1034 "-1" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534558 true] [17592186295328 1111 #uuid "bc5f625b-06cc-53be-a1c6-e3d112cd2a75" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295330 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1089 "q-77152" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1100 "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1113 #uuid "6b0d4192-2013-565b-ac9f-79ea30bb05ae" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295329 1145 "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =16 \\\\ a & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-4.$" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295331 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295332 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295333 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295334 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186295335 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1041 "selection" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1104 #edb/ref 17592186295333 13194139534558 true] [17592186295330 1110 #uuid "f58711c7-ccbd-558a-a2f7-105490661a59" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295331 1034 "-9" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534558 true] [17592186295331 1111 #uuid "539ce263-6b84-5cbd-abef-7e7369f00338" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295332 1034 "-8" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295332 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534558 true] [17592186295332 1111 #uuid "c8da9be2-1d42-5429-9acf-21ee85a2e9ef" 13194139534558 true] [17592186295333 1034 "-4" 13194139534558 tr